  "text": "Nearly 300,000 H-1B renewals this year, a record. While the front door gets smaller, the back corridor is booming. New H-1B slots? Capped at 85,000. But renewals? No cap at all. Employers are keeping every worker they have. Indians hold 72-75% of all H-1B visas. Tech, engineering, consulting, they are the backbone. Each extension costs employers $2,000 to $5,000. Multiply that by 291,000. Hundreds of millions spent just to hold on. But here is the trap. Every renewal keeps you working. But none of them advance your green card. The EB-2 wait for Indians? 37 years. 65% of US companies say they have lost skilled foreign workers. The system is breaking for everyone. Working is possible. Belonging is not. That is the paradox 500,000 Indian professionals live with every day.",
